  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 1129 AM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nA fairly calm week is expected across our forecast area. Weak \nridging builds in across the state for Monday and Tuesday, which \nallows temperatures to continue to climb. A few areas, primarily in \neastern NM, may get back to 70F by Tuesday afternoon. The only \nnotable weather feature is likely to happen Tuesday night/Wednesday \nmorning in the form of a backdoor front pushing into eastern NM. \nTroughing across the central and upper Great Plains looks to break \ndown and send this front towards us. At the moment, this front does \nnot appear to be robust, with only brief gusts between 25-35mph \nfavored. However, will need to watch where the 700mb jet is forecast \nto be, as if it's further west towards the NM/TX border as the GFS \nwould like to suggest, this may increase winds along and behind the \nfront. After Wednesday, stronger ridging looks to build in to end \nthe work week, continuing the tranquil weather conditions across the \nstate and bringing decent chances for near to above normal \ntemperatures, especially low temperatures.",
